$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Hydroxy-N-(2-oxo-2-phenyl-ethyl)-benzamide
(3a) was synthesized according to the following procedure: Salicylic acid
(1.8 mmol), thionyl chloride (3.6 mmol) and a drop of DMF were added into
dichloromethane (15 mL) and heated to reflux for 3 hours. The resulting
solution was poured into an ice bath, then sat. aq. NaHCO3 (12 mL) was
added and stirred for 1 minute. 2-aminoacetophenone hydrochloride (0.6
mmol) was added and the solution was warmed up to room temperature. After
2 hours, the solution was extracted with dichloromethane (4* 20 mL ) and
sat. aq. NaCl (20 mL), The organic layer was dry over Na2SO4, then
purified by flash chromatography on silica gel with ethyl acetate and
petroleum ether used (VEA:VPE = 4 : 1 ).
2-Hydroxy-N-[2-(4-methoxy-phenyl)-2-oxo-ethyl]-benzamide (3b). Yield: 120
mg (70%), pale yellow solid; eluent: petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (6 :
1). Mp.: 135.0-136.0 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 12.20 (s, 1H),
8.01-7.97 (m, 2H), 7.57 (dd, J = 7.9, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 7.43-7.39 (m, 1H),
7.00-6.96 (m, 3H), 6.91-6.87 (m, 1H), 4.85 (d, J = 4.1 Hz, 2H), 3.88 (s,
3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 191.9, 169.9, 164.5, 161.5, 134.4, 130.3,
127.1, 125.9, 118.8, 118.5, 114.2, 113.9, 55.6, 45.8; IR (neat) 3346,
1598, 1573, 1533, 1424, 1361, 1268, 1231, 1182, 1098, 1017, 987, 838,
752, 634, 609 (cm-1); HRMS (ESI/TOF) m/z calcd. for C16H15NO4 [M+Na]+:
308.08933, found: 308.08933.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM TBAI-Catalyzed Oxidative Cross-Coupling of Phenols and
2-Aminoacetophenones
