$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure E To a solution of an acid
(1.0 eq) in DMF (7.4 mL/mmol) were added DIPEA (4.0-5.0 eq) and HATU (1.2
eq). After 30 min at room temperature, the appropriate amine (1.3 eq) was
added and the reaction mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature.
The solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure. The residue was
partitioned between CH2Cl2 and saturated NaHCO3. The organic phase was
washed with water and brine, dried over Na2SO4, filtered and concentrated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography on silica gel to afford the desired product. Compound 39
was prepared according to the procedure E from
2-(4-ethyl-5,5,6,6-tetramethyl-2-oxomorpholin-3-yl)acetic acid (0.528
mmol), DIPEA (0.460 mL; 2.63 mmol), HATU (0.243 g; 0.639 mmol) and
4-isopropylaniline (0.087 mL; 0.651 mmol) in DMF (3.8 mL). Purification
by flash chromatography on silica gel using a gradient of EtOAc (20 to
50%) in heptane. 0.136 g of the title compound as a white powder.
2-(4-Ethyl-6,6-dimethyl-2-oxomorpholin-3-yl)-N-(3-methylbenzyl)acetamide
(84). The compound was prepared according to the procedure E from 58
(0.316 mmol), DIPEA (0.240 mL; 1.37 mmol), HATU (0.136 g; 0.358 mmol) and
3-methylbenzylamine (0.050 mL; 0.399 mmol) in DMF (2 mL). Purification by
flash chromatography on silica gel using a gradient of EtOAc (25 to 100%)
in heptane. 0.009 g (9%) of the title compound as a yellow oil.
ESI/APCI(+): 319 (M+H). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.05-7.23 (4H, m); 6.69
(1H, br s); 4.39 (2H, m); 3.37 (1H, m); 2.75-3.00 (4H, m); 2.35-2.47 (2H,
m); 2.33 (3H, s); 1.37 (3H, s); 1.36 (3H, s); 1.04 (3H, t).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 2-(2-Oxo-morpholin-3-yl)-acetamide Derivatives as Broad-Spectrum
Antifungal Agents
